huggorm-bindings carries one file it did not write.

`get-env.sh` is Nix's own script, `src/nix/get-env.sh` in the Nix
source this package links. Nix compiles it into the `nix` binary,
where no library can reach it, so a copy travels beside the bindings,
from the Nix of the same version. The copy is the text the binary
embeds: the file, after the one newline Nix's build puts before it.

Its terms are its own: the GNU Lesser General Public License v2.1,
copyright the Nix contributors (NixOS/nix). Nix's README states the
licence, and `COPYING.nix` beside the script is its text, copied from
the same Nix source. Everything else in this package is Apache-2.0,
under the umbrella LICENSE.
